All 15 tests pass. Here's what was fixed across the three modules:

**`src/auth.py`**
- `has_permission`: Changed exact string match to case-insensitive comparison using `.lower()` on both sides.
- `is_admin_or_owner`: Changed `and` to `or` — admin status or owner match should each grant access independently.

**`src/inventory.py`**
- `__init__`: Replaced mutable default argument `{}` with `None` + `dict(initial)` to prevent shared state across instances.
- `add`: Changed overwrite (`= qty`) to accumulation (`+= qty`).
- `reserve`: Changed `>=` to `>` so reserving the exact available quantity is allowed.
- `release`: Added guard to raise `ValueError` when releasing more than was reserved.

**`src/text_utils.py`**
- `slugify`: Lowercased alphanumeric characters during conversion; replaced the single `replace("--", "-")` with a `while` loop to collapse arbitrarily long runs of dashes.
- `truncate`: Subtracted `len(suffix)` from the slice so total output length respects `max_len`.
